            "show_read_more": true,
            "style": "accordions",
            "title_1": "",
            "raw_content_1": "",
            "title_2": "Why You Should Book a Strategy Session?",
            "raw_content_2": "<ul><li><strong>Investment in Success:</strong> Treat your interior design project as an investment in the success of your business. Our strategy session will help you unlock the full potential of your space, creating an environment that enhances productivity, fosters creativity, and leaves a lasting impression on clients and visitors.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Time Efficiency:</strong> Save time and streamline the design process by discussing your ideas, preferences, and goals upfront during our strategy session. By addressing key aspects of your project in a focused and efficient manner, we can accelerate the design process and get your project off to a strong start.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Risk Mitigation:</strong> Avoid costly mistakes by addressing potential challenges and design considerations early in the process. We will identify any potential pitfalls or obstacles and develop strategies to overcome them, ensuring a smooth and successful project implementation.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Clarity on Project Scope and Personalised Guidance:</strong>  strategy session will help you   explore potential design solutions that align with your vision and objectives. </li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Budget Optimisation:</strong> Cost-effective design strategies and prioritising investments that deliver the greatest impact. Our strategy session will help you make informed decisions about budget and resource allocation for your project.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Confidence in Decision-Making:</strong> Leverage our expertise and insights to give you the confidence to move forward with your project knowing that you're making the best possible decisions for your business.</li></ul>",
            "title_3": "What's Included in Hospitality Design Services?",
            "raw_content_3": "<ul><li><strong>Client Background and Hotel Vision: </strong>Understanding the client's brand vision, target market, competitive positioning, and desired guest experience for the hotel, including any unique selling points or thematic elements to be incorporated into the design.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Concept Development and Design Direction: </strong>Mood boards and design concept presentations showcasing the proposed aesthetic direction, theme, and ambiance for the hotel spaces, including guest rooms, lobby, dining areas, and common areas.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Space Planning and Layout Design: </strong>Detailed floor plans illustrating the optimal spatial arrangement of guest rooms, suites, public areas, amenities, and circulation flow within the hotel to enhance functionality, comfort, and guest experience.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>3D Renderings and Visualisation: </strong>Photorealistic 3D renderings of key areas within the hotel, such as guest rooms, lobby, restaurant, and spa facilities, providing visual representations of the proposed design concepts to stakeholders and investors.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Furniture and Fixture Specifications: </strong>Recommendations for furniture, fixtures, and equipment (FF&E) selections that marry style with functionality, ensuring durability, comfort, and aesthetic appeal while adhering to the hotel's brand identity and target market.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Branding Integration Concepts: </strong>Strategies for integrating branding elements, signage, and unique guest experiences into the hotel design to create a cohesive and memorable identity that resonates with guests and fosters loyalty.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Lighting Design Plan: </strong>Lighting layout plans and fixture selections to enhance ambiance, visibility, and mood throughout the hotel spaces, as well as acoustical treatments to mitigate noise and create a comfortable environment for guests.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Colour Palette and Material Selections: </strong>Selections of colors, textures, and materials for flooring, wall finishes, upholstery, and decorative elements that evoke the desired atmosphere and reflect the hotel's style, luxury, and sophistication.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Custom Millwork and Cabinetry Designs: </strong>Designs for custom millwork, cabinetry, and built-in features tailored to the unique needs and branding of the hospitality venue, providing storage solutions and enhancing the overall design aesthetic.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Guest Comfort and Accessibility: </strong>Considerations for guest comfort, accessibility, and safety, including ADA compliance, universal design principles, and ergonomic considerations to accommodate diverse guest needs and preferences.</li></ul>",
            "title_4": "Benefits of Investing in Your Business",
            "raw_content_4": "<ul><li><strong>Represent Your Brand:</strong> A well-designed workplace can boost employee morale, satisfaction, and retention, leading to a happier and more engaged workforce.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Boost Employee Morale:</strong> A well-designed workplace can boost employee morale, satisfaction, and retention, leading to a happier and more engaged workforce.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Enhance Productivity:</strong> By optimising the office layout and environment, we'll help maximise employee productivity and efficiency, leading to improved business performance.</li></ul><p></p><ul><li><strong>Attract Top Talent:</strong> A visually appealing and functional workspace can attract top talent and impress clients, enhancing your company's reputation and competitive edge in the market.</li></ul>",
            "title_5": "",
            "raw_content_5": "",
            "padding_bottom": 32
          }
        },
